# Line endings.
#
# This is a Windows-primary repo whose git installs `core.autocrlf=true` in the
# SYSTEM config (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig). That setting checks files
# out as CRLF while storing them as LF, which is invisible until something
# writes a file back — then a diff appears that is 100% line-ending churn with
# no content change. 187 tracked files were sitting in that state (index LF,
# worktree CRLF) when this file was added.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes the checkout match what is stored, so the working
# tree stops disagreeing with the index. The index was already LF throughout,
# so this needs no `git add --renormalize` and produces no tree-wide
# normalization commit — the existing history is already correct.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The two exceptions that must stay CRLF: Windows batch and PowerShell.
# cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat files (a label or a multi-line block can be
# read past its terminator), and PowerShell's signature blocks are CRLF-
# sensitive. Both are executed by Windows tooling, not read by git.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
